        "title": "config: accept per-agent elevatedDefault overrides and complete per-agent verbose/elevated flow (#73680)",
        "body": "## Summary\n\nMakes a **per-agent `elevatedDefault`** actually work, and completes per-agent\n`verboseDefault` flow in the reply path (issue #73680).\n\n## The gap\n\nOn current `main`, the runtime already reads a per-agent `elevatedDefault`\n(directive resolution + status surfaces) and the docs document it, **but**:\n- `AgentEntrySchema` does not include `elevatedDefault`, so config validation\n  silently rejects/strips a per-agent `elevatedDefault`.\n- `resolveAgentConfig` never populates `elevatedDefault` (unlike `verboseDefault`).\n- The reply directive resolution reads only `agentCfg.elevatedDefault` (the global\n  default) and `agentCfg.verboseDefault`, skipping the per-agent `agentEntry`\n  layer that `reasoningDefault` already uses.\n\nNet effect: a documented per-agent `elevatedDefault` had no effect.\n\n## The fix\n\n- Add `elevatedDefault` to the per-agent config type (`AgentConfig`) and\n  `AgentEntrySchema`, with schema help + label entries.\n- Resolve it in `resolveAgentConfig` as `entry.elevatedDefault ?? defaults.elevatedDefault`,\n  mirroring `verboseDefault`.\n- In `resolveCurrentDirectiveLevels` and `resolveReplyDirectives`, read\n  `agentEntry.elevatedDefault` (and `agentEntry.verboseDefault`) as the per-agent\n  layer between session overrides and the global default — the same precedence\n  `reasoningDefault` already uses (`session ?? agentEntry ?? global`). Elevated\n  resolution stays gated by `elevatedAllowed`, so this does not widen when elevated\n  output is disallowed.\n- Regenerate the config doc baseline hash for the new key.\n\n`verboseDefault`'s per-agent schema landed on `main` independently since this PR\nwas opened; this revision drops the now-redundant schema bits and keeps the still\n-missing `elevatedDefault` schema plus the per-agent verbose/elevated fallback in\nthe directive path. Rebased onto current `main`.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/agents/agent-scope.test.ts src/auto-reply/reply/directive-handling.levels.test.ts src/config/config.schema-regressions.test.ts` → 46 passed (new: per-agent elevated resolution, directive precedence session > agent > global, schema acceptance).\n- `node --import tsx scripts/generate-config-doc-baseline.ts --check` → OK.\n- `pnpm tsgo:core` and `pnpm tsgo:test:src` → clean. `oxfmt --check` / `oxlint` clean.\n\nCloses #73680\n",
        "branch": "fix/73680-per-agent-verbose-elevated-defaults",
